<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liejiaomi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2nd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liejiaomi was a ruler (kunmo) of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wusun">Wusun</a> in the 2nd century BCE. According to the Han histories he was raised among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xiongnu-empire">Xiongnu</a> after his father was killed, and he later led the Wusun west to the Ili valley and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/issyk-kul">Issyk-Kul</a> basin, driving out the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuezhi">Yuezhi</a>. In old age he received the Han envoy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhang-qian">Zhang Qian</a> and married the Han princess <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liu-xijun">Liu Xijun</a>, beginning the Wusun alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> against the Xiongnu.</p></div>
